  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 1.Biblioteca
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: Biblioteca
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.51364, y: 35.89837}
  firstPartInfo: 'Valletta is awash with lights and sounds; a brittle glamour that
    dances off the walls and glances off the cracks in the stones. Gentrification
    sticks to the surfaces with its price-tagged promise. I wonder how this city
    of merchants with its flashy allure developed this veneer. The crevices in the
    old stone, unreached by artificial lights, seem to have another story to tell
    - shadows slipping into dilapidation.  I am at the Bibliotheca because I am determined
    to pursue another side of Valletta, a side that this newfound extravagance has
    tried its best to conceal - a history of poverty and hardship whose legacy lingers
    beyond/behind the glitzy facades '
  secondPartInfo: "In an article by Evelyn Pullicino [<link=https://www.um.edu.mt/library/oar/handle/123456789/18107><u><color=blue>Link</link></u></color>
    ], I learn about a young thief who pleaded that poverty had led him to crime.
    The article suggests that the law\u2019s attitude to poverty was, at best, ambivalent:
    \u2018Poverty might have been perceived as a reasonable motivation for stealing
    but it was not considered a redeeming excuse in the Maltese Criminal Court.\u2019
    I am curious to learn the outcome of the case. The boy would have travelled from
    Vittoriosa to Valletta by boat, where he would be formally questioned and charged.  
    I need to go outside the city walls, through a gate that carries a queen\u2019s
    name, and walk down to a quay overlooked by a church. "
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Poverty
  hintOfPOI: The quay looks across at the city of Vittoriosa, otherwise known as
    Birgu.
  solutionOfPOI: "I need to go down to Grand Harbour, to Quarry Wharf \u2013 where,
    these days, the ferry from the Three Cities docks."
